== TWO SEEDS STILL ESCAPE, AND THAT IS STRUCTURAL, NOT A GAP TO PATCH ==
  SEED 4, empty-query guard: websearch_to_tsquery('english','   ') yields an EMPTY tsquery
  and 'tsv @@ ' matches nothing, so the database refuses a blank search whether or not we
  do. No fixture can make this discriminate. The guard is belt-and-braces; the test's claim
  is downgraded in place to what it actually proves.
  SEED 5, explicit user_id predicate: RLS is already bound by runAsUser and carries the
  isolation alone, so deleting the predicate changes nothing observable. The test proves
  THE BOUNDARY HOLDS -- the invariant that matters -- not the predicate. Nothing driven
  through runAsUser could prove the latter. The policy itself is watched red in
  scripts/redproof-user-corpus-rls.mjs.
